## Network Resilience: The Circuit Breaker Pattern

Mobile connections drop frequently. The enterprise standard requires that all remote network calls use a **Circuit Breaker** to avoid cascading socket timeouts and drain device battery:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Breaker["Circuit Breaker States"]
        Closed["1. Closed (Normal)\nAll requests pass through"]
        Open["2. Open (Tripped)\nFails immediately to cache"]
        HalfOpen["3. Half-Open (Testing)\nTests probe request"]

        Closed -->|"Failure threshold exceeded"| Open
        Open -->|"Reset timeout expires"| HalfOpen
        HalfOpen -->|"Probe succeeds"| Closed
        HalfOpen -->|"Probe fails"| Open
    end

